※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=5301
※ pl4g-test: args -shared
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5301 LANG_HOST_PARAMETER_TYPE

※ What a function the host defines is handed is what C has.  A record not
※ marked `@[abi]` is laid out as this compiler lays it out, which nothing
※ compiled by something else could read, so it does not cross.

type Point =
    x : i64 ; y : i64

@[host("takes_a_point")]
fn takes_a_point(both: Point) → i64

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn run() → i64:
    takes_a_point(Point(.x ← 1i64, .y ← 2i64))
